#lang r7rs
;; r7rs-lang-plan R1 / D8: `#e` on a non-integral literal would need an exact
;; rational, which the numeric stage (R5) has not brought yet.  Reading
;; `#e1.5` as the inexact 1.5 would be a wrong answer wearing the exactness
;; prefix, so the reader refuses it and names the stage that lifts the limit.
;; A literal with a non-zero fractional part on purpose: `#e1.0` is integral
;; and reads fine as the exact 1.
(defn main [] : int
  (println #e1.5)
  0)
